# "Each combat" is on either player's turn, and "you've cast" is its controller's casts alone: on turn 4 Bot2 casts two spells, so Bot2's
# Summons becomes a 3/3 Monk creature and attacks for 3, and Bot1's, whose controller cast none, stays an enchantment.
[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Reverberating Summons
Island x20
[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Reverberating Summons
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Reverberating Summons.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Reverberating Summons.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.BeginCombat]
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Reverberating Summons.Types = Enchantment; Creature
? Bot1.Battlefield.Reverberating Summons.Types = Enchantment
Bot2.Attack(Reverberating Summons > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Life = 17
[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 17
